3. When processing %3: Skips because value is empty, doesn't write prefix "\n" 
4. When processing %L: Writes prefix "\n\n" (from both skipped %2 and %3) and then the value of %L

This results in extra blank lines in the output. The fix would be to remove trailing newlines from prefixes when the corresponding field is empty.

